# This script is used to perform a differential expression analysis of publicly available data in the Gene Expression Omnibus repository
# The raw counts of each data set have been downloaded from GREIN (http://www.ilincs.org/apps/grein/)

# Aim
# This script analyzes RNA-seq datasets (e.g. GSE182018, OCI-AML2 ± HHT)
# to assess how transcript expression changes relate to RNA thermodynamic
# properties (Normalized_MFE per nucleotide and Specific_heat).
# It also evaluates curated proliferation and cell-cycle gene sets.
#
# Key Steps
# 1) Load libraries, thermodynamics table (MFE + heat capacity),
#    curated gene sets, and dataset-specific raw counts + metadata.
#
# 2) Map gene symbols/Entrez IDs to Ensembl transcript IDs (biomaRt).
#    Ensure consistency of counts and sample metadata (matching order).
#
# 3) Build DESeq2 object:
#    - Prefilter low-count transcripts (≥3 reads)
#    - Run DESeq2 differential expression (~ condition)
#    - QC checks: dispersion plot, PCA, heatmaps of sample distances.
#
# 4) Join DE results with thermodynamic annotations:
#    - Scatter plots of log2FC vs Normalized_MFE / Specific_heat
#    - Compare UP vs DOWN groups (t-test, KS, permutation test)
#    - Define “high-MFE” transcripts (75th percentile cutoff),
#      test enrichment with two-proportion z-tests.
#
# 5) Assess compositional impact:
#    - Fraction of high-MFE transcript counts in Control vs Treatment
#    - Fisher/z-tests on group differences
#
# 6) Heat capacity analysis:
#    - Compare UP vs DOWN transcripts
#    - Evaluate high-MFE subsets separately
#
# 7) Gene-level and pathway analysis:
#    - Aggregate gene counts
#    - Differential expression at gene level
#    - Filter results by curated proliferation/cell-cycle sets
#    - Summarize mean ± SD log2FC per set
#    - Generate error-bar plots and set-wise box plots
#
# Outputs
# - QC plots (PCA, sample heatmaps, dispersion)
# - Scatter/box/violin plots for MFE and Specific_heat
# - Statistics (t-tests, KS tests, permutation, z-tests)
# - Gene set summaries with mean ± SD log2FC and box plots




